From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:32:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the Mac game in focus while its window is up by default

Tears of the Kingdom and Ocarina of Time stop presenting and go silent once
they are out of focus. On the Mac, clicking into another app took the key
window, so the game froze until its window was clicked again. A player
reads that as a hang: Ocarina's log showed 'oe focus state -> 2' and no
frame after it.

DM_FOCUS_KEEP is now on by default. DM_FOCUS_KEEP=0 restores the focus
changes. Minimizing still counts as leaving the game.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: a Mac game should keep running when another app is active, as a player expects from a window
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#911
---
 dm/host/front_mac.m   | 6 +++---
 docs/env_switches.tsv | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/front_mac.m b/dm/host/front_mac.m
index 792eda42..a8f19f60 100644
--- a/dm/host/front_mac.m
+++ b/dm/host/front_mac.m
@@ -1298,9 +1298,9 @@ void front_run(void (*guest)(void)) {
         // content view by itself; only the scale factor has to be carried over to the screen the window ended up on. The screen's rate is matched in fullscreen only (screen_match_apply)
         [nc addObserverForName:NSWindowDidEnterFullScreenNotification object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; screen_refresh(win.screen); g_fullscreen = 1; g_layer.contentsScale = win.backingScaleFactor; screen_match_apply(); }];
         [nc addObserverForName:NSWindowDidExitFullScreenNotification object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; g_fullscreen = 0; screen_refresh(win.screen); g_layer.contentsScale = win.backingScaleFactor; screen_match_apply(); }];
-        // DM_FOCUS_KEEP=1 (scripts/regress.py): the game stays in focus while its window is up, whichever app is active. Tears of the Kingdom stops presenting out of focus, so
-        // another app taking the key window during an unattended run read as a hang (no frame after the last focus change)
-        static int keep = -1; if (keep < 0) keep = getenv("DM_FOCUS_KEEP") && atoi(getenv("DM_FOCUS_KEEP"));
+        // DM_FOCUS_KEEP (on by default, =0 turns it off): the game stays in focus while its window is up, whichever app is active. Tears of the Kingdom and Ocarina of Time
+        // stop presenting out of focus, so clicking into another app read as a hang (no frame and no sound after the last focus change)
+        static int keep = -1; if (keep < 0) keep = !getenv("DM_FOCUS_KEEP") || atoi(getenv("DM_FOCUS_KEEP"));
         [nc addObserverForName:NSWindowDidResignKeyNotification object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; input_release(); if (!win.miniaturized && !g_text_box && !keep) dm_focus_set(2); }];
         [nc addObserverForName:NSWindowDidBecomeKeyNotification object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; input_resume(); dm_focus_set(1); }];
         [nc addObserverForName:NSWindowDidMiniaturizeNotification object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; input_release(); dm_focus_set(3); dm_audio_suspend(1); dm_gfx_suspend(1); }];
diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index e1d163f2..33ba1115 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ DM_EXEC_OUT	path	File `oe::ExecuteProgram` records the next program and its para
 DM_EXPERIMENTAL_BUILDER	switch	`1` makes the NSP script run the extraction and the shader split through nxbuild's binaries beside `NXB_BIN` (the path of its `nxb` binary) where nxbuild supports the case, with the same outputs; any other case, an unsupported stage or an output that fails the checks runs the standard way (the Mac launcher's Use experimental builder setting)
 DM_FD_LOG	diagnostic	`=<seconds>` logs, every that many seconds, the number and kinds of file descriptors the process has open
 DM_FIXED_TIME	switch	`=<seconds>`: the user clock always returns that time and the host time zone is pinned to UTC, for deterministic comparison
-DM_FOCUS_KEEP	switch	`1` keeps the game in focus while its Mac window is up, whichever app is active (minimizing still counts); `scripts/regress.py` sets it, so another app taking the key window during a run does not pause a game that stops out of focus
+DM_FOCUS_KEEP	switch	On by default: the game stays in focus while its Mac window is up, whichever app is active (minimizing still counts). `=0` sends focus changes when another app takes the key window; `scripts/regress.py` sets it, so another app taking the key window during a run does not pause a game that stops out of focus
 DM_FONT_DIR	path	Folder of the shared-font stand-ins (`standard.ttf`, `nintendo_ext.ttf` with the button icons); the app, the Mac launcher and the NSP script set it
 DM_FORCE_STRICT	diagnostic	`=1` makes the loader fail on forced-hook entries no module references, instead of only noting them (for checking a mistyped list)
 DM_FORK_PATCHES	path	the fork patches a build carries, comma separated (build_ipa.sh and build_shell.sh read dm/fork_patches.txt into it): `DMForkPatches` in the app's Info.plist and the first log line
